## [ ] Phase 2: Surgical Sync Eradication & Production VRAM Management [NEXT]

- [ ] **2.1 Eradicate Dynamic `cudaMalloc` in Transfer Loops** (`core/src/CUDA/gpu/upload.cu`)
  - [ ] Audit and remove lines 20–28 dynamic allocation guards in `upload_to_gpu`
  - [ ] Switch temporary transfer buffers to stream-ordered memory pools (`cudaMallocAsync` / `cudaFreeAsync`)
  - [ ] Implement userspace Best-Fit with Coalescing (BFC) Caching Allocator over pre-allocated VRAM arena
- [ ] **2.2 Non-Blocking Loss Telemetry** (`core/src/CUDA/gpu/download.cu`)
  - [ ] Remove `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` from `download_loss`
  - [ ] Asynchronously copy loss via `cudaMemcpyAsync` into a dedicated 4-byte pinned host slot
  - [ ] Implement non-blocking polling via stream event query (`cudaEventQuery`), preserving double-buffered compute
- [ ] **2.3 Lock-Free SPSC Ring Buffer & Async Disk Prefetch** (`core/util/optimizer.cpp`)
  - [ ] Eliminate busy-wait spin-locks on `Portion::buffer_in_use` and `Portion::context_in_use`
  - [ ] Implement lock-free Single-Producer Single-Consumer (SPSC) ring buffer
  - [ ] Launch background producer thread to prefetch next 100,000-token chunk from disk to RAM ahead of GPU consumption
- [ ] **Gate 2 Verification:**
  - [ ] Exactly 0 calls to `cudaMalloc` or `cudaDeviceSynchronize` during active training/inference loops
  - [ ] Zero GPU starvation bubbles verified via Nsight Systems timeline trace

